cli: fix the client-steering trigger to send the caller's request

Two defects made a commanded (non-interactive) steer impossible on the CLI:

1. steer_sta ignored the caller-supplied params node and instead scraped
   `get_sta <net> 1` (the whole network dump), wrapping that as the ClientSteer
   subdoc -- so the controller received no actual steer target and emitted no
   Client Steering Request. set_ssid/set_channel already use m_param.net_node;
   make steer_sta do the same, falling back to get_sta only for the interactive
   editor (no params supplied).

2. get_edited_node() aliased a subtree of the caller's tree (the get_sta
   "Result" node) into new_node and freed it at the end, so the caller later
   double-freed it. The found_result==false branch already cloned; clone in the
   found_result==true branch too.

With these plus the tree-string buffer fix, a scripted ClientSteer JSON drives a
full BTM steer end to end (verified: client roams controller<->extender, both
ways, repeatably).

diff --git a/src/rdkb-cli/em_cmd_cli.cpp b/src/rdkb-cli/em_cmd_cli.cpp
index 41af9b5e..85eb6691 100644
--- a/src/rdkb-cli/em_cmd_cli.cpp
+++ b/src/rdkb-cli/em_cmd_cli.cpp
@@ -121,7 +121,11 @@ int em_cmd_cli_t::get_edited_node(em_network_node_t *node, const char *header, c
     for (i = 0; i < node->num_children; i++) {
         if (strncmp(node->child[i]->key, "Result", strlen("Result")) == 0) {
             found_result = true;
-			child = node->child[i];
+			/* Clone, do not alias into the caller's tree: new_node is built from
+			   child and freed at the end of this function, which would otherwise
+			   free a subtree the caller still owns and frees again (a double free).
+			   The found_result==false branch below already clones. */
+			child = em_net_node_t::clone_network_tree(node->child[i]);
             break;
         }
     }
@@ -382,9 +386,15 @@ int em_cmd_cli_t::execute(char *result)
             break;
 
         case em_cmd_type_steer_sta:
-            snprintf(in, sizeof(em_long_string_t), "get_sta %s 1", m_cmd.m_param.u.args.args[1]);
-			if ((node = m_cli.exec(in, strlen(in), NULL)) == NULL) {
-				return -1;
+			/* A caller-supplied params node (non-interactive: the web UI or a
+			   script passing a ClientSteer JSON) IS the steer request -- use it
+			   directly, the way set_ssid/set_channel use net_node. Only fall back
+			   to scraping get_sta for the interactive editor case (no params). */
+			if ((node = m_cmd.m_param.net_node) == NULL) {
+				snprintf(in, sizeof(em_long_string_t), "get_sta %s 1", m_cmd.m_param.u.args.args[1]);
+				if ((node = m_cli.exec(in, strlen(in), NULL)) == NULL) {
+					return -1;
+				}
 			}
             bevt->type = em_bus_event_type_steer_sta;
             info = &bevt->u.subdoc;
